meta {
  name: Get Client App Settings
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/settings
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: ru
}

docs {
  # Get Client App Settings

  Public endpoint. Returns the client app rules/terms of use and the call-out fee notice,
  both written in the admin panel (/settings). Use this to show the T&C screen before or
  during client registration (no auth required).

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "content": "<h1>Правила</h1><p>Текст правил пользования...</p>",
      "master_call_out_fee_note": "Если вы отмените заказ после выезда мастера, нужно оплатить выезд."
    }
  }
  ```

  `content` is raw HTML — render it in a WebView or parse it to display in the app.
  Returns empty string `""` if no rules have been configured yet.

  `master_call_out_fee_note` — plain-text notice about paying the master for the call-out
  when the client cancels an order after a master has already been assigned. Show it on the
  cancel-confirmation screen. Already resolved for the request locale: send `X-Locale: tk`
  for Turkmen, `ru` (or nothing) for Russian. Falls back to the Russian text when the
  Turkmen one is empty, and is `""` when nothing has been written yet — hide the block then.
}
